# Git Push Policy

**NEVER run `git push` automatically.** Every push to `origin/main` triggers a Vercel production build and deployment.

## Rules

- ✅ `git add`, `git commit` — fine to run when the user asks to commit
- ❌ `git push` — ALWAYS stop and ask the user first

## Required behaviour

After committing, always ask the user before pushing:

> "Ready to push — this will trigger a Vercel build. Want me to push now?"

Only run `git push` after the user explicitly says yes (e.g. "yes", "push it", "go ahead").

## Why

- Vercel rebuilds and redeploys on every push to `main`
- Unnecessary pushes waste build minutes and can deploy half-finished work
- The user wants full control over when a deployment happens
